@startuml
title CAMARA Brand Registration API and Verified Caller usage flow
autonumber "<font color=blue><b>[00]"
hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

participant CC as "**API consumer**\nCall Center Platform"
box "Operator network"
  participant APIGW as "API Gateway\nExposure"
  participant BRAND as "Brand Registration\nService"
  participant VC as "Verified Caller\nService"
  participant CSCF as "Voice\nnetwork"
end box
participant SINK as "Consumer notification\nendpoint (sink)"

== Authentication and onboarding ==
note over CC,APIGW
  Obtain an access token according to the CAMARA Security and Interoperability Profile.
  Required scopes: brand-registration:create/read/update/delete or verified-caller:create.
  The exact authorization flow is agreed during onboarding.
end note

== Create Brand Registration ==
CC -> APIGW: **POST /registrations**\nAuthorization: Bearer token\nx-correlator (optional)
activate APIGW
note right of APIGW
  JSON body: CreateOrUpdateRegistrationRequest

  Required properties:
  • phoneNumber — registered caller number in international E.164 format.
  • displayName — brand text shown to the called party (max. 32 characters).
  • terminatingCountryCode — country calling code of the called number (integer 1–999).

  Optional properties:
  • phoneNumberAlternate — an alternate phone number, also in E.164 format.
  • expiresAt — registration expiry date, YYYY-MM-DD (RFC 3339 / ISO 8601 date).
  • displayAsset — URI for a visual asset such as a logo, image or video; may use IMS-style URI parameters. Display depends on provider/device support.
  • customerId — unique customer identifier for the brand (max. 64 characters).
  • verifyCallerAction — anti-spoofing action if caller verification fails:
    BLOCK_UNVERIFIED blocks the call; DO_NOT_BRAND allows it without branding.
    If omitted, this feature is not enabled.
  • campaignName — logical campaign name grouping numbers under a brand (max. 64 characters).
  • callPurpose — purpose classification; e.g. Customer-Service, Survey,
    Telemarketing, Debt-Collection, Charity, Informational, Do-Not-Originate.
  • sink — HTTPS URL receiving event notifications (max. 2048 characters).
  • sinkCredential — credentials used by the provider to authenticate callback delivery;
    credentialType can be ACCESSTOKEN or PRIVATE_KEY_JWT.

  Request bodies with undeclared properties are rejected
  with 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT.
end note
APIGW -> BRAND: Create registration
activate BRAND
BRAND --> APIGW: **201 Created**\nRegistrationRecord
APIGW --> CC: **201 Created**\nRegistrationRecord
deactivate BRAND
deactivate APIGW

note over CC,BRAND
  Response fields can include registrationId, status, createdAt, updatedAt,
  expiresAt, quota, quotaThreshold and sink. sinkCredential is not returned.
end note

== Read registrations ==
opt List registrations
  CC -> APIGW: **GET /registrations**\nQuery parameters (all optional)
  note right of APIGW
    Filters:
    • customerId — filter by enterprise/brand owner identifier, within the authenticated client's own registrations.
    • displayName — filter by registered display name.
    • status — filter by registration status.
    • createdAt.lte / createdAt.gte — creation timestamp less than/equal to or greater than/equal to the supplied timestamp.
    • updatedAt.lte / updatedAt.gte — last-update timestamp less than/equal to or greater than/equal to the supplied timestamp.
    • expiresAt — filter by expiry date.
    • terminatingCountryCode — filter by called-party country code.
    • callPurpose — filter by call-purpose classification.
    • page / perPage — pagination controls.

    Providers may support a subset of recommended filters.
    Multiple filters are combined with logical AND.
    Results are restricted to registrations owned by the authenticated client.
  end note
  APIGW -> BRAND: Query registrations
  BRAND --> APIGW: **200 OK / 206 Partial Content**\nRegistrationRecords + pagination
  APIGW --> CC: Results + pagination\n(204 No Content if empty)
end

opt Read one registration
  CC -> APIGW: **GET /registrations/{registrationId}**
  note right of APIGW
    registrationId — unique identifier of the existing registration
    (path parameter; max. 256 characters).
  end note
  APIGW -> BRAND: Read registration by ID
  BRAND --> APIGW: **200 OK** RegistrationRecord
  APIGW --> CC: RegistrationRecord
end

== Update Brand Registration ==
opt Replace an existing registration
  CC -> APIGW: **PUT /registrations/{registrationId}**\nJSON body: CreateOrUpdateRegistrationRequest
  note right of APIGW
    registrationId — unique identifier of the registration to update (path parameter).
    The request body uses the same properties and descriptions as POST /registrations.
    Required: phoneNumber, displayName, terminatingCountryCode.
    Optional: phoneNumberAlternate, expiresAt, displayAsset, customerId,
    verifyCallerAction, campaignName, callPurpose, sink, sinkCredential.
  end note
  APIGW -> BRAND: Replace registration
  BRAND --> APIGW: **200 OK** RegistrationRecord
  APIGW --> CC: Updated RegistrationRecord
end

== Delete Brand Registration ==
opt Delete an existing registration
  CC -> APIGW: **DELETE /registrations/{registrationId}**
  note right of APIGW
    registrationId — unique identifier of the registration to delete
    (path parameter; max. 256 characters).
  end note
  APIGW -> BRAND: Delete registration
  BRAND --> APIGW: **204 No Content**
  APIGW --> CC: **204 No Content**
end

== Call pre-announcement (Verified Caller API) ==
opt If a call pre-announcement is required
  CC -> APIGW: **POST /pre-announce**\nAuthorization: Bearer token\nScope: verified-caller:create\nx-correlator (optional)
  APIGW -> VC: Create pre-announcement\nJSON request
  activate VC
  note right of VC
    Required:
    • callingParticipant — registered caller phone number (E.164).
    • calledParticipant — destination phone number (E.164).

    Optional:
    • strategy — verification method: BRAND_DISPLAY or SMS.
      If omitted, the provider chooses a default; SMS is reserved for future use.
    • timeToLive — validity duration in seconds (1–86400); provider may enforce bounds or a different value.
    • registrationId — UUID identifying the registered brand information.
    • dynamicDisplayName — call-specific display name overriding the registered brand (max. 32 characters; BRAND_DISPLAY only).
    • callReason — call-specific reason shown in addition to the brand (max. 32 characters; BRAND_DISPLAY only).

    Unknown JSON properties are rejected with 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT.
  end note
  alt Created with response body
    VC --> APIGW: **201 Created**\nAnnouncementInfo\npreAnnouncementId (optional UUID)\nexpiresAt (optional RFC 3339 timestamp)
    APIGW --> CC: **201 Created**\nAnnouncementInfo
  else Created without response body
    VC --> APIGW: **204 No Content**
    APIGW --> CC: **204 No Content**
  end
  deactivate VC
  note over CC,VC
    The call must be placed before expiresAt to be eligible for verification.
    The provider may return the effective expiry if it differs from the requested timeToLive.
    The provider is advised to verify only one call per pre-announcement.
    Documented responses include 400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422, 429, 500 and 503.
  end note
end

== Call branding ==
CC -> CSCF: **INVITE**\n\
  FROM: calling number\n\
  TO: called number\n\
  X-VERIFIED: preAnnouncementId
activate CSCF

CSCF -> VC: **GET /pre-announce**\n\
  callingParticipant\n\
  calledParticipant\n\
  preAnnouncementId
activate VC

note over VC, CSCF
  Validate the pre-announcement context,
  its validity period and the calling/called numbers.
end note

alt pre-announced and verified
  VC --> CSCF: **200 OK**\n\
    preAnnouncementId\n\
    verification: VERIFIED

  CSCF -> BRAND: Check registration and retrieve branding\n\
    calling number
  activate BRAND
  BRAND --> CSCF: **200 OK**\n\
    displayName\n\
    displayAsset
  deactivate BRAND

  CSCF -> CSCF: **INVITE**\n\
    calling number\n\
    called number\n\
    RCD (branding)\n\
    <size:30><&circle-check>

  CSCF -> VC: **Inform**\nBranding successfully performed

  opt Registration configured with sink URL
    VC -> SINK: **POST {sink}**\nContent-Type: application/cloudevents+json\nCloudEvent notification
    note right of SINK
      Event types:
      • call-branded
      • status-changed
      • quota-threshold-reached
      • quota-exhausted

      sinkCredential configures callback authentication:
      ACCESSTOKEN or PRIVATE_KEY_JWT.
    end note
    SINK --> VC: **204 No Content**
  end

else continue - Not branded
  VC --> CSCF: **200 OK**\n\
    verification: NOT_VERIFIED\n\
    verifyCallerAction: DO_NOT_BRAND
  CSCF -> CSCF: **INVITE**\n\
    calling number\n\
    called number

else blocked
  VC --> CSCF: **200 OK**\n\
    verification: NOT_VERIFIED\n\
    verifyCallerAction: BLOCK_UNVERIFIED
  CSCF-\\: <color:red>**BLOCKED INVITE**
end

deactivate VC
deactivate CSCF

note over CC,BRAND
  Consult the OpenAPI specifications and CAMARA common files for complete error details.
  x-correlator is an optional correlation header where documented.
end note
@enduml
